.TH CKMUX 1 "August 25, 2026" "ckmux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ckmux \- terminal multiplexer with a visible desktop interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ckmux
.br
.B ckmux ls
.br
.B ckmux new
.RB [ \-s " name" ]
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B ckmux attach
.RB [ \-\-share ]
.RB [ \-\-watch ]
.RB [ \-\-adopt\-size ]
.I name|id
.br
.B ckmux kill\-session
.I name|id
.br
.B ckmux check\-config
.br
.B ckmux kill\-server
.br
.B ckmux
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ckmux
keeps terminal sessions and the programs inside them alive when its client
disconnects. A detached per-user server owns the sessions, pseudo-terminals,
screen state, scrollback, and window layout. The client presents that state as
a visible ckVision desktop with menus, a context-sensitive footer, and movable
terminal windows.
.PP
Running
.B ckmux
starts the server if necessary and opens the session picker. Detaching or
losing the client connection leaves every child program running. Reattaching
shows current state rather than replaying output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ls
List the sessions held by an existing server. This command does not start a
server merely to report that none is running.
.TP
.BI new " [\-s name] [command]"
Create a session without attaching. If supplied,
.I command
runs in its first terminal through the configured shell.
.TP
.BI attach " [options] name|id"
Attach directly to one session. With no mode option, take the session over and
return previous readers to their pickers.
.TP
.BI kill\-session " name|id"
Ask every program in one session to end, then remove the session.
.TP
.B check\-config
Parse the configuration, print warnings and settings not honored by this
build, and start no server. Configuration warnings produce exit status 1.
.TP
.B kill\-server
End the server and every terminal it owns.
.SH ATTACH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-share
Join without evicting readers already attached.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Join read-only. Input and all session-changing operations are refused by the
server. Implies
.BR \-\-share .
.TP
.B \-\-adopt\-size
Make the session desktop the size of this screen on arrival. This reflows
windows and resizes child pseudo-terminals for every attached reader.

@CKMUX_KEY_APPENDIX@
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration is a small INI file with
.BR [general] ,
.BR [terminal] ,
.BR [printer] ,
.BR [render] ,
and
.B [keys]
sections. A missing file is normal and every setting has a built-in default.
Use
.B ckmux check\-config
to validate it without starting a server. In
.BR [keys] ,
.B bind
and
.B unbind
change prefix chords by the action names listed in the generated key section.
.PP
The browser guide documents every setting and default at
https://cklukas.github.io/ckmux/configuration.html.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CKMUX_SOCKET
Server socket path used exactly as given. Otherwise ckmux uses
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ckmux\-<uid>/default.sock
with
.B $TMPDIR
and then
.B /tmp
as fallbacks.
.TP
.B CKMUX_CONFIG
Configuration file used exactly as given. Otherwise ckmux uses
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ckmux/ckmux.conf
or ordinarily
.BR $HOME/.config/ckmux/ckmux.conf .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ckmux/ckmux.conf
Default configuration file.
.TP
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ckmux\-<uid>/default.sock
Default server socket when
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is set to an absolute path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the requested command completed. Status 1 means an understood
request could not be completed, or
.B check\-config
found configuration warnings. Status 2 means command-line arguments were
invalid.
.SH SECURITY
The server accepts only local Unix-domain socket connections from the owning
user. Child output is parsed into terminal state and re-rendered; raw child
bytes are never forwarded to the host terminal. Printing is captured into a
bounded in-memory spool and never opens a printer device or executes a print
command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR infocmp (1),
.BR tic (1),
.BR terminfo (5)
.PP
Project documentation: https://cklukas.github.io/ckmux/
